#!/bin/sh
# Agent Desktop session (runs as the unprivileged `agent` user).
# TigerVNC's Xvnc is both the X server and the VNC server; it listens only on a
# Unix socket shared with the host (no TCP port), viewed from Iron Settings.
set -eu
SOCK=/run/iron-agent/display/vnc.sock
GEOM="${IRON_AGENT_GEOMETRY:-1600x900}"
rm -f "$SOCK"
Xvnc :1 -geometry "$GEOM" -depth 24 -rfbport -1 -rfbunixpath "$SOCK" -rfbunixmode 0666 \
    -SecurityTypes None -AlwaysShared -AcceptSetDesktopSize -nolisten tcp -desktop "Iron Agent Desktop" &
XPID=$!
for _ in $(seq 1 50); do [ -S "$SOCK" ] && break; sleep 0.1; done
export DISPLAY=:1
xsetroot -solid '#0e1115' 2>/dev/null || true
[ -f /usr/share/iron-agent/wallpaper.png ] && command -v xwallpaper >/dev/null && xwallpaper --zoom /usr/share/iron-agent/wallpaper.png || true
mkdir -p "$HOME/outbox" "$HOME/workspace"
# openbox-session also starts XDG autostart entries (tint2 panel included).
openbox-session &
sleep 1
xterm -title "Agent shell" -geometry 120x32+40+40 -e bash -l &
wait $XPID
